00:40:57,831 --> 00:41:00,640
It's so nice that we can divide up the tasks when we meet up.

1032
00:41:00,641 --> 00:41:02,011
(As her friends clean up, )

1033
00:41:03,241 --> 00:41:06,141
(Si Hyeon takes out mysterious food.)

1034
00:41:06,841 --> 00:41:08,881
- Is that duteoptteok? - Yes.

1035
00:41:09,911 --> 00:41:13,751
(A few hours ago, Si Hyeon prepared the filling and rice cake.)

1036
00:41:14,781 --> 00:41:19,291
(She wrapped the filling with rice cake.)

1037
00:41:19,721 --> 00:41:21,641
This is the same as the Dubai chewy cookie, DCC.

1038
00:41:23,131 --> 00:41:24,731
I think it's the K-DCC...

1039
00:41:25,031 --> 00:41:26,901
that contains pine nuts and chestnuts.

1040
00:41:27,061 --> 00:41:28,200
K-DCC.

1041
00:41:28,201 --> 00:41:30,001
(K-DCC, duteoptteok)

1042
00:41:30,101 --> 00:41:32,201
- Did you make duteoptteok? - Yes.

1043
00:41:32,301 --> 00:41:34,201
It was So Yeon's birthday.

1044
00:41:35,711 --> 00:41:39,741
(The duteoptteok cake is complete.)

1045
00:41:40,011 --> 00:41:43,911
(Embarrassed)

1046
00:41:44,381 --> 00:41:46,251
(Happy birthday to you.)

1047
00:41:48,421 --> 00:41:50,021
- Thank you. - Happy birthday.

1048
00:41:50,751 --> 00:41:52,060
I haven't received rice cake...

1049
00:41:52,061 --> 00:41:53,321
- in a long while. - Really?

1050
00:41:53,721 --> 00:41:55,121
Will you make the dessert now?

1051
00:41:55,491 --> 00:41:56,561
Make a quenelle.

1052
00:41:57,631 --> 00:41:59,531
- Shall I scoop it out for everyone? - Yes.

1053
00:42:01,661 --> 00:42:04,171
(Pushing)

1054
00:42:05,301 --> 00:42:06,301
(Impressed)

1055
00:42:06,841 --> 00:42:08,301
It looks like a quail egg.

1056
00:42:08,441 --> 00:42:09,510
I know.

1057
00:42:09,511 --> 00:42:11,711
(The shape of the ice cream is extraordinary.)

1058
00:42:12,911 --> 00:42:14,741
- Why is it so funny? - It looks pretty.

1059
00:42:14,911 --> 00:42:16,251
- It's a bit. - It's pretty.

1060
00:42:16,951 --> 00:42:18,750
(Yogurt and daeng yuzu ice cream)

1061
00:42:18,751 --> 00:42:20,851
- She made it pretty with a spoon. - I know.

1062
00:42:21,481 --> 00:42:22,761
Louis Vuitton sure is different.

1063
00:42:23,721 --> 00:42:26,021
The shape is called a quenelle.

1064
00:42:26,721 --> 00:42:28,660
For people who make desserts,

1065
00:42:28,661 --> 00:42:31,031
it's a source of pride like the chefs' knife skills.

1066
00:42:31,361 --> 00:42:32,460
That's right.

1067
00:42:32,461 --> 00:42:33,901
- Thank you. - You made it well.

1068
00:42:34,231 --> 00:42:36,130
It looks nice, right? This one is the best.

1069
00:42:36,131 --> 00:42:37,900
(So Yeon made an incredibly pretty quenelle.)

1070
00:42:37,901 --> 00:42:38,941
It's tasty.

1071
00:42:39,371 --> 00:42:40,800
(She puts a spoonful of class into her mouth.)

1072
00:42:40,801 --> 00:42:41,911
I bought it.

1073
00:42:42,341 --> 00:42:43,441
I feel great.

1074
00:42:44,141 --> 00:42:45,171
I'll eat this.

1075
00:42:46,881 --> 00:42:49,081
(It looks tasty.)

1076
00:42:49,351 --> 00:42:50,511
How is it?

1077
00:42:50,811 --> 00:42:53,581
I like how the big grains with chestnut pieces provide texture.

1078
00:42:53,881 --> 00:42:55,290
(I'm glad that they're eating well.)

1079
00:42:55,291 --> 00:42:57,120
When I talk to them,

1080
00:42:57,121 --> 00:42:59,321
I learn so many new things.

1081
00:42:59,561 --> 00:43:01,621
The more I dig, the more I find new things.

1082
00:43:01,721 --> 00:43:03,791
It makes me go back...

1083
00:43:04,191 --> 00:43:06,001
to my initial enthusiasm.

1084
00:43:06,601 --> 00:43:08,930
With cabbage, you can make soup, kimchi,

1085
00:43:08,931 --> 00:43:11,571
seasoned vegetables, and jeon.

1086
00:43:12,641 --> 00:43:15,411
I want to be an all-rounder.

1087
00:43:15,871 --> 00:43:17,171
Shall I be Cabbage Guru?

1088
00:43:17,471 --> 00:43:18,911
(Laughing)

1089
00:43:19,081 --> 00:43:20,681
- The last glass. - The last glass.

1090
00:43:21,241 --> 00:43:23,681
- Thank you for the invitation. - Thank you for coming.

1091
00:43:28,991 --> 00:43:31,650
(The Journey of Little Tiger Who Is Still Eager to Learn)

1092
00:43:31,651 --> 00:43:33,491
We enjoyed the video.

1093
00:43:34,891 --> 00:43:37,731
I could tell why she was called Little Tiger.

1094
00:43:37,991 --> 00:43:40,861
From watching the video, I could feel her daring spirit.

1095
00:43:41,001 --> 00:43:43,631
She has the face of a baby and the heart of a tiger.

1096
00:43:43,831 --> 00:43:46,741
When you become crazy about one thing,

1097
00:43:46,901 --> 00:43:48,171
you gain formidable strength.

1098
00:43:48,401 --> 00:43:50,510
She has always been crazy about edible greens.

1099
00:43:50,511 --> 00:43:52,880
- She'll be a big tiger soon. - That's right.

1100
00:43:52,881 --> 00:43:54,140
- Thank you. - Nice.

1101
00:43:54,141 --> 00:43:55,650
It can't be easy.

1102
00:43:55,651 --> 00:43:57,151
She's really cool.

1103
00:43:58,351 --> 00:44:01,720
Si Hyeon showed us Little Tiger's unexpected daily life.

1104
00:44:01,721 --> 00:44:03,790
We'll root for her so that she can charge forward.

1105
00:44:03,791 --> 00:44:05,821
- Thank you. - Thank you.

1106
00:44:06,461 --> 00:44:07,591
(I Live Alone)

1107
00:44:07,691 --> 00:44:10,331
(New Footprints)

1108
00:44:10,991 --> 00:44:13,501
(Walking)

1109
00:44:14,001 --> 00:44:15,230
(She hurries her steps to go somewhere.)

1110
00:44:15,231 --> 00:44:16,831
Where is she going so busily?

1111
00:44:19,001 --> 00:44:21,541
She isn't here yet.

1112
00:44:24,871 --> 00:44:28,311
(Ja Yeon waits for someone at the apartment's resting area.)

1113
00:44:28,541 --> 00:44:30,851
(Looking around)

1114
00:44:31,911 --> 00:44:33,051
Hye Won!

1115
00:44:34,151 --> 00:44:35,281
(Who is it?)

1116
00:44:35,521 --> 00:44:37,791
Hello. Isn't it cold?

1117
00:44:39,261 --> 00:44:40,921
What are you making to need this?

1118
00:44:42,261 --> 00:44:43,691
- It's a secret. - A secret?

1119
00:44:44,091 --> 00:44:45,931
- Thank you. - Is it a Karrot transaction?

1120
00:44:46,601 --> 00:44:48,061
It's huge.

1121
00:44:48,871 --> 00:44:50,271
Why do you have it at home?

1122
00:44:50,931 --> 00:44:52,141
It isn't a Karrot transaction.

1123
00:44:52,541 --> 00:44:54,981
There's a group chat room for the residents of the apartment.

1124
00:44:55,071 --> 00:44:57,271
People give away free items...

1125
00:44:57,511 --> 00:45:00,741
and lend the items...

1126
00:45:00,881 --> 00:45:02,151
others need.

1127
00:45:02,451 --> 00:45:03,750
The neighbors must be close.

1128
00:45:03,751 --> 00:45:05,650
- There's still neighborly love. - Yes.

1129
00:45:05,651 --> 00:45:07,757
- The neighbors are friendly. - It's like that in Namyangju.

1130
00:45:07,781 --> 00:45:10,220
No way. I'll use them well and bring them back to you.

1131
00:45:10,221 --> 00:45:11,891
It's nice to see neighbors do that.

1132
00:45:12,261 --> 00:45:13,420
Is your cat doing well?

1133
00:45:13,421 --> 00:45:15,861
- My cat adjusted well. - I'm curious.

1134
00:45:16,061 --> 00:45:18,190
- Please upload some photos. - Okay.

1135
00:45:18,191 --> 00:45:19,360
There's also a group chat room for cat owners.

1136
00:45:19,361 --> 00:45:20,361
Gosh!

1137
00:45:20,362 --> 00:45:22,282
- A group chat for cat owners. - That's so cute.

1138
00:45:22,401 --> 00:45:23,701
- I'll see you later. - Right.

1139
00:45:25,501 --> 00:45:27,641
There should be one more.

1140
00:45:29,811 --> 00:45:30,971
Hi!

1141
00:45:31,741 --> 00:45:32,910
Ha Jin!

1142
00:45:32,911 --> 00:45:34,040
(Another neighbor brought a different kitchen utensil.)

1143
00:45:34,041 --> 00:45:35,240
It's a child.

1144
00:45:35,241 --> 00:45:37,851
Is that child part of the community as well?

1145
00:45:38,011 --> 00:45:40,080
- It must be a chore. - His mom must have told him to go.

1146
00:45:40,081 --> 00:45:41,851
Thank you!

1147
00:45:42,521 --> 00:45:44,390
What are you doing with this?

1148
00:45:44,391 --> 00:45:46,061
I'm planning to make something.

1149
00:45:47,421 --> 00:45:49,307
I'll make something nice and send it back to you.

1150
00:45:49,331 --> 00:45:50,531
That's great to see.

1151
00:45:50,631 --> 00:45:52,430
Ta-da! Give this jam to your mom.

1152
00:45:52,431 --> 00:45:54,201
(She returns the favor with the jam.)

1153
00:45:54,701 --> 00:45:56,731
Thank you for coming out.

1154
00:45:57,231 --> 00:45:58,231
Bye!

1155
00:45:58,232 --> 00:45:59,541
(Bowing)

1156
00:46:00,701 --> 00:46:03,101
(After carrying the warmth of the neighbors in both hands, )

1157
00:46:03,371 --> 00:46:06,741
(she returns home with a light heart.)

1158
00:46:10,651 --> 00:46:11,851
Bom!

1159
00:46:12,921 --> 00:46:14,051
Hey, Bom!

1160
00:46:14,151 --> 00:46:16,150
- It's a dog-like cat! - Are you here, Bom?

1161
00:46:16,151 --> 00:46:17,850
Isn't that a cat we've never seen before?

1162
00:46:17,851 --> 00:46:19,720
- I'm back. - It's a baby cat.

1163
00:46:19,721 --> 00:46:21,621
- Bom? - Her name is Bom.

1164
00:46:22,361 --> 00:46:23,791
She's the second cat in the house.

1165
00:46:24,091 --> 00:46:25,191
I see.

1166
00:46:25,291 --> 00:46:28,300
She's a very bright and curious...

1167
00:46:28,301 --> 00:46:29,571
dog-like cat.

1168
00:46:30,801 --> 00:46:33,071
(Bom, second cat)

1169
00:46:33,141 --> 00:46:34,741
- She's so pretty. - She's pretty.

1170
00:46:35,771 --> 00:46:37,311
She's still a baby.

1171
00:46:37,571 --> 00:46:39,510
I was walking with my friend in December...

1172
00:46:39,511 --> 00:46:41,641
and my friend spotted a cat.

1173
00:46:41,711 --> 00:46:44,850
I noticed the cat as well, but it started running right toward me.

1174
00:46:44,851 --> 00:46:45,980
It was a stray cat.

1175
00:46:45,981 --> 00:46:47,581
When I saw it from up close,

1176
00:46:48,021 --> 00:46:49,491
there was a wound on its back.

1177
00:46:50,191 --> 00:46:52,991
I thought an emergency treatment would be enough,

1178
00:46:53,621 --> 00:46:55,020
but I was told surgery was required.

1179
00:46:55,021 --> 00:46:57,230
The wound on its back...

1180
00:46:57,231 --> 00:46:59,201
was decaying.

1181
00:46:59,261 --> 00:47:00,961
After letting it go under surgery,

1182
00:47:01,661 --> 00:47:04,431
I went the next day.

1183
00:47:05,701 --> 00:47:06,841
The doctor asked me...

1184
00:47:07,971 --> 00:47:09,911
if I knew more about the cat.

1185
00:47:10,041 --> 00:47:11,841
Apparently, the cat was blind...

1186
00:47:12,711 --> 00:47:16,311
and was in pain.

1187
00:47:17,581 --> 00:47:18,821
Gosh, that poor cat.

1188
00:47:19,451 --> 00:47:21,320
Her eyes look very healthy from afar.

1189
00:47:21,321 --> 00:47:22,621
They look fine from here.

1190
00:47:22,991 --> 00:47:25,690
It had a visual impairment without an external injury...

1191
00:47:25,691 --> 00:47:29,061
and it would be hard to find an owner.

1192
00:47:29,631 --> 00:47:33,161
That was why I decided to bring her home to raise her...

1193
00:47:33,831 --> 00:47:35,361
and she stayed still in my lap.

1194
00:47:35,771 --> 00:47:37,101
That would feel touching.

1195
00:47:37,231 --> 00:47:40,570
As if we were destined to meet, we met each other on my birthday.

1196
00:47:40,571 --> 00:47:41,840
- Gosh. - On your birthday?

1197
00:47:41,841 --> 00:47:44,047
- You two were destined to meet. - You two were destined to meet.

1198
00:47:44,071 --> 00:47:45,210
The two cats are getting along with each other.

1199
00:47:45,211 --> 00:47:47,581
Chacha was very cautious at the start,

1200
00:47:47,711 --> 00:47:49,671
but the two really get along with each other now.

1201
00:47:50,651 --> 00:47:52,850
I think it took around two weeks for Chacha to open up to her.

1202
00:47:52,851 --> 00:47:54,251
The vet said...

1203
00:47:54,651 --> 00:47:57,350
the cat wouldn't have survived through winter...

1204
00:47:57,351 --> 00:47:58,820
and be able to see spring come...

1205
00:47:58,821 --> 00:48:01,091
if I didn't bring the cat.

1206
00:48:01,291 --> 00:48:04,590
I wanted the cat's life...

1207
00:48:04,591 --> 00:48:06,230
to be full of spring...

1208
00:48:06,231 --> 00:48:08,031
and that was why I named her Bom.

1209
00:48:09,631 --> 00:48:10,871
She met a great owner.

1210
00:48:11,201 --> 00:48:14,171
But there are no inconveniences for her in everyday life.

1211
00:48:14,301 --> 00:48:17,141
Her other sense are very developed...

1212
00:48:17,811 --> 00:48:19,610
and she remembers where everything is in the house.

1213
00:48:19,611 --> 00:48:21,241
- Really? - She can move around freely.

1214
00:48:21,411 --> 00:48:23,181
- She moves with her other senses. - Right.

1215
00:48:23,711 --> 00:48:24,981
What about the litter box?

1216
00:48:25,451 --> 00:48:27,621
She didn't know how to use the litter box at first.

1217
00:48:27,681 --> 00:48:29,151
She just went anywhere.

1218
00:48:29,321 --> 00:48:30,590
That was why I kept teaching her.

1219
00:48:30,591 --> 00:48:33,421
When she was about to poop, I moved her to the litter box.

1220
00:48:33,491 --> 00:48:36,691
I did that for a few days while catching her poop with my hands...

1221
00:48:36,761 --> 00:48:38,330
and she got used to it.

1222
00:48:38,331 --> 00:48:40,011
- She's fine with it now. - What a relief.

1223
00:48:40,301 --> 00:48:41,861
Gosh, are you happy to see me?

1224
00:48:43,831 --> 00:48:45,000
Come in.

1225
00:48:45,001 --> 00:48:47,041
- She's so cute. - Good job.

1226
00:48:47,471 --> 00:48:49,611
I'll pet you after washing my hands.

1227
00:48:51,093 --> 00:48:52,363
Chacha!

1228
00:48:54,503 --> 00:48:56,373
Mom's here, Chacha.

1229
00:48:56,408 --> 00:48:57,748
She's always there.

1230
00:48:57,948 --> 00:48:59,318
Do you want to sleep more?

1231
00:49:01,988 --> 00:49:02,988
Okay.

1232
00:49:02,989 --> 00:49:04,217
(It's hard to see the first daughter's face.)

1233
00:49:04,218 --> 00:49:06,157
You got another cat while raising one cat.

1234
00:49:06,158 --> 00:49:08,157
Isn't it hard to raise two cats?

1235
00:49:08,158 --> 00:49:09,827
Are you used to it now?

1236
00:49:09,828 --> 00:49:12,527
Having two cats doesn't make it harder.

1237
00:49:12,528 --> 00:49:14,127
My friend that rescued Chacha...

1238
00:49:14,128 --> 00:49:16,997
takes care of them whenever I get too busy.

1239
00:49:16,998 --> 00:49:18,338
That's a relief.

1240
00:49:18,968 --> 00:49:20,098
Bom!

1241
00:49:20,738 --> 00:49:22,368
They can't be that long.

1242
00:49:23,268 --> 00:49:24,408
She's just like her mother.

1243
00:49:25,038 --> 00:49:26,077
Here.

1244
00:49:26,078 --> 00:49:28,108
(Is she biting the cat treat with her mouth?)

1245
00:49:28,708 --> 00:49:30,308
(Sniffing)

1246
00:49:31,408 --> 00:49:33,978
This was a method you came up with to cut her nails.

1247
00:49:34,948 --> 00:49:37,018
She goes wild if I don't do that.

1248
00:49:37,588 --> 00:49:40,088
(Luring her with the cat treat in her mouth)

1249
00:49:42,588 --> 00:49:44,827
(Don't cut my nails.)

1250
00:49:44,828 --> 00:49:46,698
(Cat treat!)

1251
00:49:48,928 --> 00:49:51,668
She's positioned perfectly as she does it so often.

1252
00:49:51,898 --> 00:49:53,367
As she's from Seoul National University,

1253
00:49:53,368 --> 00:49:55,867
she smartly came up with the position.

1254
00:49:55,868 --> 00:49:58,308
She's biting onto the cat treat and you bring up her school?

1255
00:49:59,678 --> 00:50:02,078
I would've never come up with that kind of position.

1256
00:50:02,608 --> 00:50:04,577
(Growling)

1257
00:50:04,578 --> 00:50:06,378
- She doesn't like it. - She doesn't like it.

1258
00:50:06,578 --> 00:50:07,678
She wouldn't like it.

1259
00:50:08,178 --> 00:50:09,917
But the cat treat must be good.

1260
00:50:09,918 --> 00:50:12,464
She has to have the cat treat, but she's also mad about her nails.

1261
00:50:12,488 --> 00:50:15,658
(She starts focusing on the treat while complaining.)

1262
00:50:16,558 --> 00:50:18,528
(Growling)

1263
00:50:18,598 --> 00:50:19,828
"Growl."

1264
00:50:20,758 --> 00:50:22,327
- I'm done. - Since she hates cutting her nails,

1265
00:50:22,328 --> 00:50:23,627
I've tried many different methods.

1266
00:50:23,628 --> 00:50:25,067
Cat treats work the best.

1267
00:50:25,068 --> 00:50:26,268
(Entranced)

1268
00:50:26,638 --> 00:50:29,108
She sounds like an evil spirit if I don't give her the treat.

1269
00:50:29,168 --> 00:50:31,208
- We're done. - Gosh.

1270
00:50:31,538 --> 00:50:33,608
(The sound of an evil spirit?)

1271
00:50:34,078 --> 00:50:36,407
- You're so fiery. - Show her an actual evil spirit.

1272
00:50:36,408 --> 00:50:38,617
- Did you get mad? - She'll behave right away.

1273
00:50:38,618 --> 00:50:39,648
Right away.

1274
00:50:40,178 --> 00:50:43,687
We still managed to get it done all at once. What a surprise!

1275
00:50:43,688 --> 00:50:44,918
(Feeling proud)

1276
00:50:45,118 --> 00:50:46,118
Go down!

1277
00:50:46,119 --> 00:50:47,587
(She took care of her nails without much trouble.)

1278
00:50:47,588 --> 00:50:49,628
The photo is here, Bom!

1279
00:50:52,258 --> 00:50:54,028
Gosh! Look at this!

1280
00:50:54,228 --> 00:50:57,227
Bom! This is you and Chacha.

1281
00:50:57,228 --> 00:50:58,798
- Did you take it yourself? - Yes.

1282
00:50:59,668 --> 00:51:01,297
I love taking photos.

1283
00:51:01,298 --> 00:51:02,778
(Oktographer's work is full of cats.)

1284
00:51:03,768 --> 00:51:04,967
(She puts the photo into a frame.)

1285
00:51:04,968 --> 00:51:06,208
Gosh, it looks so nice.

1286
00:51:07,938 --> 00:51:09,147
(Did it come out nicely?)

1287
00:51:09,148 --> 00:51:10,248
How cute!

1288
00:51:12,478 --> 00:51:13,978
- That's so cute. - That's so cute.

1289
00:51:15,288 --> 00:51:17,518
(A standing ovation for herself)

1290
00:51:17,788 --> 00:51:19,718
- All right. - I should give that a try.

1291
00:51:20,088 --> 00:51:21,617
What? Take a picture of a burger and put it up?

1292
00:51:21,618 --> 00:51:23,088
No. Take a picture with Kkotbun.

1293
00:51:23,528 --> 00:51:24,627
A burger!

1294
00:51:24,628 --> 00:51:26,897
Hey, why are you treating him like a beast?

1295
00:51:26,898 --> 00:51:30,598
Why would I put up a picture of a burger?

1296
00:51:30,698 --> 00:51:32,638
- Since you love burgers. - Right.

1297
00:51:35,208 --> 00:51:38,108
(She gets up with a big plastic sheet.)

1298
00:51:38,508 --> 00:51:41,308
(She spreads it out on top of the table.)

1299
00:51:44,308 --> 00:51:45,578
What is she doing?

1300
00:51:47,648 --> 00:51:49,848
(Picking up)

1301
00:51:50,348 --> 00:51:51,687
(She gets things out from the bag.)

1302
00:51:51,688 --> 00:51:53,758
She must be getting ready to cook.

1303
00:51:56,458 --> 00:51:57,657
(Makgeolli and flour?)

1304
00:51:57,658 --> 00:52:00,058
- Makgeolli and flour? - Makgeolli and flour.

1305
00:52:01,358 --> 00:52:03,368
Isn't she making jeon to have with the makgeolli?

1306
00:52:03,598 --> 00:52:04,827
That sounds nice.

1307
00:52:04,828 --> 00:52:05,938
- Right? - Yes.

1308
00:52:07,898 --> 00:52:11,307
(The table is full of ingredients and kitchen utensils.)

1309
00:52:11,308 --> 00:52:13,178
Since Seollal is approaching,

1310
00:52:13,478 --> 00:52:16,247
I wanted to make gifts for the people around me.

1311
00:52:16,248 --> 00:52:18,077
I'm planning to make some gaeseong juak.

1312
00:52:18,078 --> 00:52:20,638
- Gosh, that was hot for a while. - She will actually make that?

1313
00:52:20,978 --> 00:52:23,347
I've always loved gaeseong juak.

1314
00:52:23,348 --> 00:52:24,947
I think it has been around 3 to 4 years.

1315
00:52:24,948 --> 00:52:28,058
The grain syrup has cinnamon and ginger in it.

1316
00:52:28,558 --> 00:52:31,357
It seeps out once you take a bite.

1317
00:52:31,358 --> 00:52:32,358
I love that taste.

1318
00:52:32,359 --> 00:52:34,128
The glutinous rice is really chewy as well.

1319
00:52:34,228 --> 00:52:35,598
Isn't it like a donut?

1320
00:52:35,668 --> 00:52:38,098
It's in between a yakgwa and a donut.

1321
00:52:38,168 --> 00:52:39,467
I remember seeing that before.

1322
00:52:39,468 --> 00:52:41,737
There was definitely a time when that was trending.

1323
00:52:41,738 --> 00:52:43,567
- Right. Around two years ago? - I remember...

1324
00:52:43,568 --> 00:52:45,007
- hearing that term. - Juak.

1325
00:52:45,008 --> 00:52:46,307
- Gaeseong juak. - Gaeseong juak.

1326
00:52:46,308 --> 00:52:47,477
Many people gave that as gifts.

1327
00:52:47,478 --> 00:52:48,577
Have you tried that before?

1328
00:52:48,578 --> 00:52:49,648
I haven't.

1329
00:52:50,008 --> 00:52:51,407
- Have you tried that before? - Me?

1330
00:52:51,408 --> 00:52:52,478
I haven't.

1331
00:52:52,748 --> 00:52:53,847
Why am I the only one who has tried it...

1332
00:52:53,848 --> 00:52:54,977
when the Gen MZers haven't?

1333
00:52:54,978 --> 00:52:56,147
I've tried it as well.

1334
00:52:56,148 --> 00:52:57,288
Gosh!

1335
00:52:58,348 --> 00:52:59,757
She's making that at home?

1336
00:52:59,758 --> 00:53:00,858
How is that made at home?

1337
00:53:00,958 --> 00:53:02,528
It doesn't need that many ingredients.

1338
00:53:02,888 --> 00:53:04,787
But it must be hard to make at home.

1339
00:53:04,788 --> 00:53:05,857
Right.

1340
00:53:05,858 --> 00:53:08,458
I find it fascinating that she thought about making that at home.

1341
00:53:10,868 --> 00:53:13,137
(She washes her hands cleanly first.)

1342
00:53:13,138 --> 00:53:15,338
(Peeking)

1343
00:53:16,368 --> 00:53:18,838
(She picks up the sheet of paper that was on the fridge.)

1344
00:53:19,878 --> 00:53:24,177
I got close with the cafe owner who sells gaeseong juak.

1345
00:53:24,178 --> 00:53:25,617
I was given the cafe owner's recipe,

1346
00:53:25,618 --> 00:53:28,298
so I think things will work out well by just following that recipe.

1347
00:53:29,048 --> 00:53:31,488
(Shall I begin now?)

1348
00:53:32,558 --> 00:53:35,758
(She boldly squeezes out the rice syrup first.)

1349
00:53:36,528 --> 00:53:39,498
(A generous amount)

1350
00:53:41,428 --> 00:53:42,627
- There's the cinnamon. - There's the cinnamon.

1351
00:53:42,628 --> 00:53:44,968
I love cinnamon and ginger.

1352
00:53:45,098 --> 00:53:46,568
I love sujeonggwa as well.

1353
00:53:47,838 --> 00:53:50,338
(She slices up a generous amount of ginger as well.)

1354
00:53:51,108 --> 00:53:52,678
It's exactly what Ja Yeon likes.

1355
00:53:55,238 --> 00:53:56,308
Next.

1356
00:53:56,608 --> 00:53:59,278
With things like grain syrup, water, honey,

1357
00:53:59,578 --> 00:54:01,418
ginger, and cinnamon,

1358
00:54:01,818 --> 00:54:03,948
they get boiled together for around 30 minutes.

1359
00:54:04,948 --> 00:54:06,418
(Beeping)

1360
00:54:07,088 --> 00:54:09,428
(She sets a timer to 30 minutes so that she won't forget.)

1361
00:54:10,088 --> 00:54:12,158
(She grabs the glutinous rice flour.)

1362
00:54:13,428 --> 00:54:15,227
(A decent amount of glutinous rice flour...)

1363
00:54:15,228 --> 00:54:17,098
(and flour get mixed together.)

1364
00:54:19,038 --> 00:54:20,098
Done.

1365
00:54:21,038 --> 00:54:22,038
There we go.

1366
00:54:22,268 --> 00:54:25,007
I do have a strainer at home,

1367
00:54:25,008 --> 00:54:26,608
but it isn't as big as that one.

1368
00:54:27,038 --> 00:54:29,878
It was nice to be able to borrow it as I was only going to use it once.

1369
00:54:30,508 --> 00:54:31,807
(I'm going to spin around as well.)

1370
00:54:31,808 --> 00:54:33,128
- She's so cute. - She's so cute.

1371
00:54:33,218 --> 00:54:34,318
She's a baby.

1372
00:54:34,718 --> 00:54:35,748
Okay.

1373
00:54:36,718 --> 00:54:39,088
(She shakes the makgeolli.)

1374
00:54:39,918 --> 00:54:41,258
Around 100ml of makgeolli.

1375
00:54:41,388 --> 00:54:43,587
- So makgeolli is used. - I add hot water...

1376
00:54:43,588 --> 00:54:44,757
for hot water kneading.

1377
00:54:44,758 --> 00:54:46,058
Hot water kneading?

1378
00:54:46,628 --> 00:54:48,727
Making a dough with hot water is called hot water kneading.

1379
00:54:48,728 --> 00:54:49,868
Is that so?

1380
00:54:50,128 --> 00:54:52,137
I think Lee Jung has never seen that word before.

1381
00:54:52,138 --> 00:54:53,337
- Totally. - It's like...

1382
00:54:53,338 --> 00:54:54,767
she's learning a new language.

1383
00:54:54,768 --> 00:54:55,838
Hot water kneading.

1384
00:54:58,568 --> 00:55:02,608
I didn't want it to be too mushy. I wanted it to be like fresh cheese.

1385
00:55:03,108 --> 00:55:05,278
I wanted it to be squeaky.

1386
00:55:07,018 --> 00:55:09,688
(The dough is ready. It's time to shape them.)

1387
00:55:10,618 --> 00:55:12,518
(Rolling)

1388
00:55:13,358 --> 00:55:16,828
(She is very focused with making the shape.)

1389
00:55:17,988 --> 00:55:21,628
(The living room is filled with just the sound of the dough.)

1390
00:55:21,998 --> 00:55:25,128
Ja Yeon is always quiet when she does these things.

1391
00:55:25,268 --> 00:55:27,267
- Others might turn on music or... - Right.

1392
00:55:27,268 --> 00:55:28,708
- Or sing. - Exactly.

1393
00:55:28,968 --> 00:55:31,068
- She does sing, though. - Okdel.

1394
00:55:31,868 --> 00:55:32,908
Right.

1395
00:55:33,278 --> 00:55:36,908
(Okdel sings her heart out while playing the piano.)

1396
00:55:38,348 --> 00:55:39,548
I quit singing.

1397
00:55:39,778 --> 00:55:41,078
I miss Okdel so much.

1398
00:55:42,188 --> 00:55:44,618
(Today, she is quietly focused on cooking.)

1399
00:55:45,388 --> 00:55:47,958
(She uses both hands this time.)

1400
00:55:48,518 --> 00:55:50,828
(Working hard)

1401
00:55:51,788 --> 00:55:52,857
I made around 30 to 40 of them.

1402
00:55:52,858 --> 00:55:54,697
Doing that many times was quite tough.

1403
00:55:54,698 --> 00:55:55,768
Definitely.

1404
00:55:57,198 --> 00:55:58,427
What's that?

1405
00:55:58,428 --> 00:56:00,797
This feels like a scene in "Surprise Mystery TV."

1406
00:56:00,798 --> 00:56:01,967
(This feels like a scene in "Surprise Mystery TV.")

1407
00:56:01,968 --> 00:56:03,037
It turns out not to be flour.

1408
00:56:03,038 --> 00:56:04,267
- It's something like bone ash. - Right.

1409
00:56:04,268 --> 00:56:05,367
(It's something like bone ash.)

1410
00:56:05,368 --> 00:56:06,877
"Why was she rolling that together?"

1411
00:56:06,878 --> 00:56:07,938
"However!"

1412
00:56:08,638 --> 00:56:10,048
"After her new cat came..."

1413
00:56:10,678 --> 00:56:11,748
"False!"

1414
00:56:13,178 --> 00:56:14,477
(She works hard to make the dough...)

1415
00:56:14,478 --> 00:56:15,618
(for the surprise gift.)

1416
00:56:15,818 --> 00:56:16,848
This is the last one.

1417
00:56:19,488 --> 00:56:20,888
The last one looks very pretty.

1418
00:56:22,018 --> 00:56:24,658
(Round)

1419
00:56:25,698 --> 00:56:27,098
(Letting out a breath)

1420
00:56:27,958 --> 00:56:29,327
(The dough looks round and smooth.)

1421
00:56:29,328 --> 00:56:31,008
- She did a great job. - They look pretty.

1422
00:56:31,728 --> 00:56:33,268
(Poking)

1423
00:56:34,068 --> 00:56:35,708
A hole is made in the dough.

1424
00:56:36,008 --> 00:56:37,838
That helps it get cooked to the inside.

1425
00:56:46,578 --> 00:56:48,498
- That must be delicious. - That smells so good.

1426
00:56:49,648 --> 00:56:52,258
The dough must be fried next.

1427
00:56:52,658 --> 00:56:54,958
(She uses the wok she borrowed from her neighbor.)

1428
00:56:55,528 --> 00:56:58,188
(Oh, right!)

1429
00:57:01,498 --> 00:57:02,528
What?

1430
00:57:02,898 --> 00:57:05,497
If there's water on the dough,

1431
00:57:05,498 --> 00:57:06,738
- it can pop up. - Right.

1432
00:57:06,868 --> 00:57:09,937
It has to be boiled up to 135°C.

1433
00:57:09,938 --> 00:57:11,538
The temperature was really important.

1434
00:57:12,478 --> 00:57:13,978
Stop at 135°C.

1435
00:57:16,378 --> 00:57:17,407
Oh, gosh!

1436
00:57:17,408 --> 00:57:18,607
(As she's about to make them...)

1437
00:57:18,608 --> 00:57:19,678
I feel nervous.

1438
00:57:21,518 --> 00:57:23,417
- Is this your first attempt? - I felt so nervous. Yes.

1439
00:57:23,418 --> 00:57:24,447
Your first attempt.

1440
00:57:24,448 --> 00:57:27,187
It looks hard to do for someone who hasn't tried it before.

1441
00:57:27,188 --> 00:57:29,288
- It looks hard to make. - Right.

1442
00:57:30,288 --> 00:57:32,657
(She carefully places them into the oil.)

1443
00:57:32,658 --> 00:57:34,458
(Nervous)

1444
00:57:34,758 --> 00:57:36,967
From 100°C to 120°C,

1445
00:57:36,968 --> 00:57:39,197
I let them get cooked slowly.

1446
00:57:39,198 --> 00:57:40,867
So they aren't fried right away at once.

1447
00:57:40,868 --> 00:57:42,838
I was told that doing that ruins their shape.

1448
00:57:43,068 --> 00:57:44,608
So the temperature is very important.

1449
00:57:47,208 --> 00:57:48,408
It looks fine.

1450
00:57:49,378 --> 00:57:51,607
Having these many bubbles means it's going well.

1451
00:57:51,608 --> 00:57:53,947
(Flipping)

1452
00:57:53,948 --> 00:57:55,048
This one flipped.

1453
00:57:55,888 --> 00:57:57,418
Okay. That's perfect.

1454
00:57:57,948 --> 00:57:59,158
It's going really well.

1455
00:58:00,558 --> 00:58:01,817
Since I'm hungry,

1456
00:58:01,818 --> 00:58:02,857
(I should have something while it fries.)

1457
00:58:02,858 --> 00:58:03,987
I'll have something simple.

1458
00:58:03,988 --> 00:58:05,658
(I should have something while it fries.)

1459
00:58:06,128 --> 00:58:07,357
(Scrubbing)

1460
00:58:07,358 --> 00:58:08,358
It's an apple.

1461
00:58:09,398 --> 00:58:11,398
(She adds an apple into the juicer.)

1462
00:58:13,698 --> 00:58:14,768
What is that?

1463
00:58:14,868 --> 00:58:15,938
- Yam. - Yam?

1464
00:58:17,238 --> 00:58:19,177
Half of it. Just this much.

1465
00:58:19,178 --> 00:58:21,278
(She puts in the exact amount she wants.)

1466
00:58:22,178 --> 00:58:23,178
Walnuts.

1467
00:58:24,908 --> 00:58:25,977
(She heads to her plant shelf.)

1468
00:58:25,978 --> 00:58:27,278
(Amazed)

1469
00:58:27,518 --> 00:58:28,947
Can you do that as an owner of plants?

1470
00:58:28,948 --> 00:58:29,987
Well...

1471
00:58:29,988 --> 00:58:31,188
(Chuckling)

1472
00:58:31,888 --> 00:58:33,287
(She cuts some of the kale she raised.)

1473
00:58:33,288 --> 00:58:34,288
Look at the leaves.

1474
00:58:35,388 --> 00:58:38,458
(She washes the kale cleanly.)

1475
00:58:40,198 --> 00:58:42,867
(After adding in a lot of healthy ingredients, )

1476
00:58:42,868 --> 00:58:44,528
(she turns the power on.)

1477
00:58:45,668 --> 00:58:48,908
(It turns into a juice nicely.)

1478
00:58:51,338 --> 00:58:55,077
(Pouring out)

1479
00:58:55,078 --> 00:58:57,307
- The juice comes out right away. - Right. I love that moment.

1480
00:58:57,308 --> 00:58:58,448
(Refreshing)

1481
00:58:59,218 --> 00:59:00,348
Gosh, this is so convenient.

1482
00:59:03,288 --> 00:59:05,187
(She drinks the natural ingredients as a juice right away.)

1483
00:59:05,188 --> 00:59:06,688
(Satisfied)

1484
00:59:11,558 --> 00:59:12,728
Since it's a juice,

1485
00:59:13,428 --> 00:59:14,827
it's easy to take in fruit and vegetables.

1486
00:59:14,828 --> 00:59:16,828
(It's easy to take in fruit and vegetables.)

1487
00:59:20,368 --> 00:59:22,138
I've been using the juicer these days...

1488
00:59:22,238 --> 00:59:24,507
and it tastes really nice and healthy.

1489
00:59:24,508 --> 00:59:26,507
(It tastes really nice and healthy.)

1490
00:59:26,508 --> 00:59:27,677
I should try that.

1491
00:59:27,678 --> 00:59:28,878
- It must be healthy. - Right.

1492
00:59:28,978 --> 00:59:30,078
With burgers?

1493
00:59:30,808 --> 00:59:32,817
- Right. - Try having burgers like that.

1494
00:59:32,818 --> 00:59:33,847
- Sung Hwan. - "With burgers."

1495
00:59:33,848 --> 00:59:36,087
- It will mince everything. - Strain out the meat juice.

1496
00:59:36,088 --> 00:59:37,208
(Strain out the meat juice.)

1497
00:59:37,448 --> 00:59:39,357
I really want to try the juice from the meat juicer.

1498
00:59:39,358 --> 00:59:40,617
- The meat juicer? - The meat juicer?

1499
00:59:40,618 --> 00:59:41,618
Gosh.

1500
00:59:41,619 --> 00:59:43,127
- Gosh! - Wait!

1501
00:59:43,128 --> 00:59:44,187
That's not what I meant!

1502
00:59:44,188 --> 00:59:45,527
I want to use the juicer...

1503
00:59:45,528 --> 00:59:47,127
with vegetables.

1504
00:59:47,128 --> 00:59:48,357
- Just have fruit and vegetables. - Right.

1505
00:59:48,358 --> 00:59:49,597
I think it will make me much healthier.

1506
00:59:49,598 --> 00:59:51,267
- It will bring down my cholesterol. - Right.

1507
00:59:51,268 --> 00:59:52,268
I'm going to try that, no matter what.

1508
00:59:52,269 --> 00:59:53,738
- It's really good. - It looks good.

1509
00:59:55,168 --> 00:59:56,368
They're finding their colors.

1510
00:59:58,978 --> 01:00:00,208
That's going to be a success.

1511
01:00:01,778 --> 01:00:03,208
(Peeking)

1512
01:00:05,608 --> 01:00:07,048
(Plopping up and down)

1513
01:00:07,918 --> 01:00:09,847
- Gosh, she's so cute! - What?

1514
01:00:09,848 --> 01:00:11,118
She's doing okay, right?

1515
01:00:12,018 --> 01:00:14,018
- That's how she sleeps. - She's doing Pilates.

1516
01:00:15,288 --> 01:00:17,988
(Shall I start taking them out now?)

1517
01:00:21,398 --> 01:00:22,958
She looks like someone with experience.

1518
01:00:23,768 --> 01:00:26,138
It must not be that hard to make at home.

1519
01:00:26,268 --> 01:00:27,838
It wasn't that hard.

1520
01:00:28,438 --> 01:00:30,167
- Didn't she just make it look easy? - Right.

1521
01:00:30,168 --> 01:00:32,377
- She's just good at this. - Right.

1522
01:00:32,378 --> 01:00:33,878
(Feeling shy)

1523
01:00:35,878 --> 01:00:36,908
They turned out nicely.

1524
01:00:38,178 --> 01:00:39,178
(Crunch)

1525
01:00:39,678 --> 01:00:41,478
- Check out the sound. - Check out the sound.

1526
01:00:41,678 --> 01:00:42,747
It must be really good.

1527
01:00:42,748 --> 01:00:43,918
(They were cooked nicely.)

1528
01:00:45,088 --> 01:00:46,718
(Picking up)

1529
01:00:47,458 --> 01:00:49,018
The grain syrup shouldn't be like that.

1530
01:00:49,158 --> 01:00:51,688
Gosh, it shouldn't be like that.

1531
01:00:52,088 --> 01:00:54,127
- What has gone wrong? - Has the grain syrup gone wrong?

1532
01:00:54,128 --> 01:00:56,167
- Is it too thick? - Can I use this?

1533
01:00:56,168 --> 01:00:57,408
(The grain syrup is too thick.)

1534
01:00:58,068 --> 01:01:00,638
(Thick)

1535
01:01:00,868 --> 01:01:02,938
It should be watery. Why has it become like this?

1536
01:01:03,268 --> 01:01:06,278
Well, when the grain syrup...

1537
01:01:06,708 --> 01:01:09,808
is scooped up like this, it should drip down.

1538
01:01:10,278 --> 01:01:13,018
But it became too thick.

1539
01:01:13,278 --> 01:01:15,078
I was wondering what went wrong.

1540
01:01:16,688 --> 01:01:19,558
(Let's still give it a try.)

1541
01:01:20,088 --> 01:01:21,187
(Mixing)

1542
01:01:21,188 --> 01:01:22,487
What's wrong about that?

1543
01:01:22,488 --> 01:01:23,687
- But... - It looks fine.

1544
01:01:23,688 --> 01:01:25,588
Isn't it fine if it tastes good?

1545
01:01:26,958 --> 01:01:29,498
(Rattling)

1546
01:01:30,398 --> 01:01:31,797
(Hitting)

1547
01:01:31,798 --> 01:01:32,958
That was the sound of a rock.

1548
01:01:34,598 --> 01:01:36,808
(She takes a bite of it mixed with the grain syrup.)

1549
01:01:42,308 --> 01:01:44,878
(Ja Yeon calls someone.)

1550
01:01:46,518 --> 01:01:47,548
Hello?

1551
01:01:47,718 --> 01:01:49,788
- Ma'am! - Hi.

1552
01:01:50,448 --> 01:01:52,458
I tried making the juak.

1553
01:01:53,688 --> 01:01:56,088
Is rice syrup different from grain syrup?

1554
01:01:57,088 --> 01:01:58,327
- Yes. - They're different, aren't they?

1555
01:01:58,328 --> 01:01:59,827
- They're different? - I see.

1556
01:01:59,828 --> 01:02:02,228
I used rice syrup.

1557
01:02:02,768 --> 01:02:03,798
Oh, dear.

1558
01:02:04,328 --> 01:02:05,768
It's really sticky.

1559
01:02:06,268 --> 01:02:08,667
The syrup is way too thick.

1560
01:02:08,668 --> 01:02:10,028
It's really thick. Check this out.

1561
01:02:10,438 --> 01:02:12,068
They won't move at all.

1562
01:02:12,908 --> 01:02:13,978
I ruined it.

1563
01:02:15,178 --> 01:02:17,207
I got one thing wrong from the recipe.

1564
01:02:17,208 --> 01:02:18,508
It was a really important part.

1565
01:02:19,278 --> 01:02:23,117
I had to buy grain syrup, but I bought rice syrup instead.

1566
01:02:23,118 --> 01:02:26,787
The key point of gaeseong juak is for the sweet syrup...

1567
01:02:26,788 --> 01:02:28,758
to flow inside...

1568
01:02:29,128 --> 01:02:31,187
and it must seep out after taking a bite.

1569
01:02:31,188 --> 01:02:32,498
- Just like that. - Moist.

1570
01:02:32,628 --> 01:02:35,498
But as I used rice syrup...

1571
01:02:36,528 --> 01:02:38,097
- It became a candied snack. - Right.

1572
01:02:38,098 --> 01:02:39,598
- Right? - It became a candied snack.

1573
01:02:40,038 --> 01:02:41,558
Let's just call it the gaeseong candy.

1574
01:02:42,238 --> 01:02:43,668
Gaeseong candy.

1575
01:02:44,138 --> 01:02:46,437
But the inside... Oh, it didn't seep in.

1576
01:02:46,438 --> 01:02:47,808
Right. The syrup didn't seep in.

1577
01:02:48,108 --> 01:02:50,348
- But how did it taste? - It tasted nice,

1578
01:02:50,578 --> 01:02:53,818
but my favorite part of the juak is the syrup...

1579
01:02:53,948 --> 01:02:55,708
- Bursting out? - bursting out after a bite.

1580
01:02:55,778 --> 01:02:58,518
But the syrup can't seep in if it's too thick.

1581
01:02:58,648 --> 01:03:00,218
Is that why it's called that?

1582
01:03:00,458 --> 01:03:02,387
- Juak sounds like "burst." - Really?

1583
01:03:02,388 --> 01:03:03,388
Really?

1584
01:03:03,758 --> 01:03:05,527
- That's why it's gaeseong juak? - You didn't know?

1585
01:03:05,528 --> 01:03:06,658
"Gaeseong juak."

1586
01:03:08,158 --> 01:03:09,267
That's not true!

1587
01:03:09,268 --> 01:03:10,697
- Oh, that's not true? - I thought it was that.

1588
01:03:10,698 --> 01:03:12,068
(That's not true?)

1589
01:03:12,168 --> 01:03:13,697
Was I too much like a Gen MZer?

1590
01:03:13,698 --> 01:03:14,897
(Was I too much like a Gen MZer?)

1591
01:03:14,898 --> 01:03:15,908
"Juak!"

1592
01:03:16,768 --> 01:03:18,508
Instead of feeling like juak,

1593
01:03:19,678 --> 01:03:21,054
it turned out to be more like tanghulu.

1594
01:03:21,078 --> 01:03:22,078
(Hitting)

1595
01:03:23,478 --> 01:03:25,377
I did so well with the dough.

1596
01:03:25,378 --> 01:03:27,418
It's okay. Just go with that.

1597
01:03:27,618 --> 01:03:29,618
It will be okay if they are eaten right away.

1598
01:03:30,348 --> 01:03:31,388
Okay.

1599
01:03:31,948 --> 01:03:34,118
You did well. You really did.

1600
01:03:34,288 --> 01:03:35,288
Okay!

1601
01:03:35,289 --> 01:03:37,258
- I'll see you soon. - Okay!

1602
01:03:39,458 --> 01:03:41,058
I did so well with their shapes.

1603
01:03:42,028 --> 01:03:43,898
I used rice syrup...

1604
01:03:45,268 --> 01:03:46,974
- and it became too sticky. - What a bummer.

1605
01:03:46,998 --> 01:03:48,037
What a bummer.

1606
01:03:48,038 --> 01:03:50,037
(Disappointed)

1607
01:03:50,038 --> 01:03:51,068
What a bummer.

1608
01:03:52,608 --> 01:03:55,078
(She still carefully takes them out so they don't stick.)

1609
01:03:56,708 --> 01:03:57,708
They're shaped so nicely.

1610
01:03:57,709 --> 01:03:59,517
They're so pretty. They look like the ones that are sold.

1611
01:03:59,518 --> 01:04:01,378
They all look the same as well.

1612
01:04:03,348 --> 01:04:05,468
Let's at least make them look nice with the toppings.

1613
01:04:07,788 --> 01:04:09,028
She's even using a forcing bag.

1614
01:04:09,488 --> 01:04:13,028
It's not the exact taste of the juak that I love,

1615
01:04:13,698 --> 01:04:15,358
but the dough came out well.

1616
01:04:15,428 --> 01:04:17,528
If I make it look nice with the toppings,

1617
01:04:17,898 --> 01:04:19,337
wouldn't it be edible?

1618
01:04:19,338 --> 01:04:21,398
(Wouldn't it be edible if I add toppings nicely?)

1619
01:04:22,298 --> 01:04:23,438
Here you go.

1620
01:04:26,208 --> 01:04:27,408
You're adding dried fruit too?

1621
01:04:28,708 --> 01:04:29,808
It's salivating.

1622
01:04:30,108 --> 01:04:31,808
(Gulping)

1623
01:04:34,348 --> 01:04:35,988
It really is pretty.

1624
01:04:36,988 --> 01:04:39,018
(Shall I put on strawberry too?)

1625
01:04:39,558 --> 01:04:41,118
(Chuckling)

1626
01:04:41,518 --> 01:04:42,628
Is it too big?

1627
01:04:44,028 --> 01:04:45,157
Will it be okay?

1628
01:04:45,158 --> 01:04:47,557
(After adding a huge strawberry...)

1629
01:04:47,558 --> 01:04:48,628
All right.

1630
01:04:50,728 --> 01:04:52,968
- It looks delicious. - It looks really delicious.

1631
01:04:53,068 --> 01:04:54,397
I love desserts.

1632
01:04:54,398 --> 01:04:55,798
(Ja Yeon's gaeseong juak is ready.)

1633
01:04:56,838 --> 01:04:59,838
(Shall I pack them now?)

1634
01:05:00,208 --> 01:05:01,508
(Putting it in)

1635
01:05:02,408 --> 01:05:03,977
(Neatly put in per topping)

1636
01:05:03,978 --> 01:05:05,547
- It's pretty. - It's really pretty.

1637
01:05:05,548 --> 01:05:06,948
It looks like juak sold at a store.

1638
01:05:09,178 --> 01:05:11,748
(After tying it neatly with a string)

1639
01:05:12,418 --> 01:05:16,458
(The Lunar New Year gift set filled with warmth is ready.)

1640
01:05:17,588 --> 01:05:18,688
All done.

1641
01:05:21,728 --> 01:05:25,898
Chacha, I'll be right back.

1642
01:05:27,468 --> 01:05:28,997
She wouldn't get out of that grandma blanket.

1643
01:05:28,998 --> 01:05:30,438
(Chacha is here.)

1644
01:05:31,138 --> 01:05:32,568
(Jumping)

1645
01:05:33,008 --> 01:05:35,377
Bom, have a good time with her.

1646
01:05:35,378 --> 01:05:36,647
(She doesn't forget to say goodbye to Bom as well.)

1647
01:05:36,648 --> 01:05:37,648
Okay?

1648
01:05:38,608 --> 01:05:41,478
(After saying goodbye to Chacha and Bom, )

1649
01:05:46,258 --> 01:05:49,558
(she takes her stuff and leaves.)

1650
01:05:52,998 --> 01:05:54,497
(She suddenly starts running.)

1651
01:05:54,498 --> 01:05:55,858
She's busy.

1652
01:05:56,828 --> 01:05:57,898
I should get there fast...

1653
01:05:58,398 --> 01:05:59,798
and practice by myself.

1654
01:06:00,038 --> 01:06:01,598
- Practice? - Practice what?

1655
01:06:02,168 --> 01:06:04,248
- She must have a gathering. - It looks like... Yes.

1656
01:06:04,708 --> 01:06:06,638
Oh, dear.

1657
01:06:06,708 --> 01:06:08,454
I feel like I know the way around her neighborhood now.

1658
01:06:08,478 --> 01:06:09,677
- This apartment complex. - If you go that way,

1659
01:06:09,678 --> 01:06:10,878
there's a basketball court...

1660
01:06:10,978 --> 01:06:12,977
- and a laundromat. - You're right.

1661
01:06:12,978 --> 01:06:15,348
I'm more familiar with her complex than my neighborhood.

1662
01:06:18,218 --> 01:06:20,578
(Where Ja Yeon passionately practiced basketball last time)

1663
01:06:21,018 --> 01:06:22,858
(She showed a shot that was close to a stunt.)

1664
01:06:23,028 --> 01:06:24,758
(Michael Okdon)

1665
01:06:25,758 --> 01:06:27,327
(She hurriedly ran to the basketball court.)

1666
01:06:27,328 --> 01:06:28,558
They're not here yet.

1667
01:06:29,328 --> 01:06:30,368
All right.

1668
01:06:31,128 --> 01:06:32,397
(Table tennis tables can be seen in the familiar court.)

1669
01:06:32,398 --> 01:06:34,598
- It's table tennis. - You can play table tennis there?

1670
01:06:34,968 --> 01:06:37,637
I got to start playing a sport I could play with others...

1671
01:06:37,638 --> 01:06:39,508
instead of basketball.

1672
01:06:40,078 --> 01:06:43,878
I'll put Michael Okdon aside for now,

1673
01:06:44,248 --> 01:06:47,147
and become Ok Table Tennis.

1674
01:06:47,148 --> 01:06:48,454
- Ok Table Tennis. - Ok Table Tennis

1675
01:06:48,478 --> 01:06:49,748
It suits her. Ok Table Tennis.

1676
01:06:49,988 --> 01:06:52,288
I joined a table tennis club this year.

1677
01:06:52,958 --> 01:06:54,364
- Table tennis is fun. - Table tennis is fun.

1678
01:06:54,388 --> 01:06:55,418
I also used to...

1679
01:06:56,158 --> 01:06:57,457
Those who went to the military have pride...

1680
01:06:57,458 --> 01:06:58,757
- in their table tennis skills. - Of course.

1681
01:06:58,758 --> 01:07:00,227
I'm the best at table tennis...

1682
01:07:00,228 --> 01:07:01,357
- Hyun Moo. - among you.

1683
01:07:01,358 --> 01:07:03,097
- I'm the best at table tennis... - Hyun Moo.

1684
01:07:03,098 --> 01:07:04,197
- among you. - Table tennis is really fun.

1685
01:07:04,198 --> 01:07:05,267
I'm almost like the Great Wall of China.

1686
01:07:05,268 --> 01:07:07,438
The Great Wall of China? I'll crush you.

1687
01:07:07,998 --> 01:07:09,097
Everyone has pride in their table tennis skills.

1688
01:07:09,098 --> 01:07:10,568
You're no match for me.

1689
01:07:10,668 --> 01:07:12,667
You can't receive my serves.

1690
01:07:12,668 --> 01:07:13,937
- I think I can. - My ball would swing past you...

1691
01:07:13,938 --> 01:07:15,007
before you even realize.

1692
01:07:15,008 --> 01:07:16,278
Well, I'd throw the ball...

1693
01:07:16,978 --> 01:07:18,607
and serve sharply like this.

1694
01:07:18,608 --> 01:07:20,077
- My serve goes sideways. - Then I'd take it with a spin.

1695
01:07:20,078 --> 01:07:21,277
Then I'd hit it back...

1696
01:07:21,278 --> 01:07:22,764
- with a backspin. - Then it'd go out.

1697
01:07:22,788 --> 01:07:23,788
(I can't believe this.)

1698
01:07:24,518 --> 01:07:25,787
My goodness.

1699
01:07:25,788 --> 01:07:27,868
(They're all burning with passion for table tennis.)

1700
01:07:29,628 --> 01:07:31,858
(I should hurry and practice.)

1701
01:07:36,058 --> 01:07:38,098
(Pulling)

1702
01:07:40,698 --> 01:07:44,738
(Installing something on the table tennis table)

1703
01:07:47,478 --> 01:07:50,008
This equipment helps you control the ball speed,

1704
01:07:50,408 --> 01:07:51,977
and it can also decide...

1705
01:07:51,978 --> 01:07:54,977
the direction of the ball when it comes out.

1706
01:07:54,978 --> 01:07:59,088
So, with this, you can practice freely.

1707
01:07:59,558 --> 01:08:01,757
That's available at your apartment complex?

1708
01:08:01,758 --> 01:08:05,088
My senior members contributed money to buy that.

1709
01:08:05,788 --> 01:08:07,158
- That machine? - Yes.

1710
01:08:08,028 --> 01:08:11,198
(Shall I warm up now?)

1711
01:08:15,038 --> 01:08:17,168
(Exhaling)

1712
01:08:18,308 --> 01:08:19,408
(Beep)

1713
01:08:19,608 --> 01:08:21,808
(Hurrying)

1714
01:08:22,308 --> 01:08:24,177
It looks like she's training for the national team.

1715
01:08:24,178 --> 01:08:26,818
- Even her attire is perfect. - I agree.

1716
01:08:27,748 --> 01:08:30,518
(Hitting)

1717
01:08:32,148 --> 01:08:35,017
Ja Yeon, you're practicing a consistent swing.

1718
01:08:35,018 --> 01:08:36,898
You need to practice until your body remembers.

1719
01:08:37,858 --> 01:08:40,858
(Focused)

1720
01:08:41,728 --> 01:08:44,497
Considering how it's been only one month for me,

1721
01:08:44,498 --> 01:08:47,998
they said I was pretty good. They're complimenting me a lot.

1722
01:08:48,238 --> 01:08:49,567
When I went on a trip with my mom,

1723
01:08:49,568 --> 01:08:51,137
there was a table tennis table at the hotel,

1724
01:08:51,138 --> 01:08:53,608
so we played together, and it was so much fun.

1725
01:08:53,978 --> 01:08:57,278
I thought it'd be nice to learn it and play with my mom.

1726
01:08:57,578 --> 01:09:00,878
I promised her I'd hone my skills next time I visit her.

1727
01:09:01,248 --> 01:09:03,548
That's why I wanted to learn to play table tennis.

1728
01:09:03,748 --> 01:09:05,087
And there happened to be a table tennis club...

1729
01:09:05,088 --> 01:09:06,417
at my apartment complex.

1730
01:09:06,418 --> 01:09:07,558
I'm the youngest member.

1731
01:09:07,918 --> 01:09:08,988
A newbie.

1732
01:09:10,888 --> 01:09:13,998
(To keep her promise with her mom, )

1733
01:09:14,958 --> 01:09:17,468
(she practices hard even by herself.)

1734
01:09:19,498 --> 01:09:21,268
(Staring fiercely)

1735
01:09:22,498 --> 01:09:23,867
(The stare of a national team table tennis player)

1736
01:09:23,868 --> 01:09:25,167
You really look like you are on the national team.

1737
01:09:25,168 --> 01:09:28,008
(The stare of a national team table tennis player)

1738
01:09:30,008 --> 01:09:32,008
- Looks like she's from Gaeseong. - Yes, a little.

1739
01:09:32,178 --> 01:09:33,724
- Looks like she's from Gaeseong. - Yes, a little.

1740
01:09:33,748 --> 01:09:34,818
Gaeseong?

1741
01:09:35,178 --> 01:09:37,624
She brought gaeseong juak as a gift for the South Korean players.

1742
01:09:37,648 --> 01:09:39,017
(She's perfectly prepared with gaeseong juak too.)

1743
01:09:39,018 --> 01:09:40,458
"Try this."

1744
01:09:40,858 --> 01:09:41,858
Her hometown food.

1745
01:09:41,859 --> 01:09:43,688
(They excitedly tease Ok Table Tennis.)

1746
01:09:44,358 --> 01:09:47,598
(Ok Table Tennis focuses without budging.)

1747
01:09:50,598 --> 01:09:51,767
She also looks like...

1748
01:09:51,768 --> 01:09:52,937
- a table tennis robot. - Yes, a little.

1749
01:09:52,938 --> 01:09:54,598
(Teasing again)

1750
01:09:55,038 --> 01:09:56,307
Your left arm...

1751
01:09:56,308 --> 01:09:57,844
- isn't in a cast, is it? - Seriously, her left arm...

1752
01:09:57,868 --> 01:09:59,148
It does look like I'm in a cast.

1753
01:09:59,878 --> 01:10:02,308
(Laughing)

1754
01:10:03,408 --> 01:10:05,254
- She does have a short arc. - She looks a bit...

1755
01:10:05,278 --> 01:10:06,977
- She does have a short arc. - She looks a bit...

1756
01:10:06,978 --> 01:10:08,377
- I look a little stiff, right? - You do look...

1757
01:10:08,378 --> 01:10:10,287
- a little stiff. - You need a bigger arc.

1758
01:10:10,288 --> 01:10:12,164
- I'm not so smooth. - You know your stuff, Jun.

1759
01:10:12,188 --> 01:10:13,217
I can tell once I see it.

1760
01:10:13,218 --> 01:10:14,288
(You're pretty good.)

1761
01:10:14,988 --> 01:10:17,857
- If you bend down a bit more... - Will I get better?

1762
01:10:17,858 --> 01:10:18,858
(Fixing)

1763
01:10:19,028 --> 01:10:20,598
You're too upright now.

1764
01:10:20,958 --> 01:10:22,504
You're too upright now. If you fix that...

1765
01:10:22,528 --> 01:10:24,144
- You're the one who's most upright. - No.

1766
01:10:24,168 --> 01:10:25,668
When you smash,

1767
01:10:25,828 --> 01:10:27,467
it needs to go up from down.

1768
01:10:27,468 --> 01:10:28,708
But she's standing too upright.

1769
01:10:29,268 --> 01:10:30,538
It needs to look like this.

1770
01:10:31,208 --> 01:10:32,644
I want to see him play table tennis.

1771
01:10:32,668 --> 01:10:34,178
(Anytime)

1772
01:10:34,878 --> 01:10:35,977
I can't do it.

1773
01:10:35,978 --> 01:10:37,848
(Grunting)

1774
01:10:38,678 --> 01:10:41,118
(Exhausted)

1775
01:10:41,718 --> 01:10:43,888
Goodness.

1776
01:10:44,318 --> 01:10:45,588
It's about time they came.

1777
01:10:47,118 --> 01:10:49,118
Gosh, you need to pick up all the balls too.

1778
01:10:49,318 --> 01:10:50,958
How can you pick them all up?

1779
01:10:52,258 --> 01:10:53,758
(Dragging)

1780
01:10:54,258 --> 01:10:56,798
(I should hurry up and clean up before they come.)

1781
01:11:00,698 --> 01:11:03,007
That's really useful. The balls go in right away.

1782
01:11:03,008 --> 01:11:04,488
(Collecting balls with a fishing net)

1783
01:11:05,038 --> 01:11:06,907
(Opening)

1784
01:11:06,908 --> 01:11:08,677
- You're here. - Hello.

1785
01:11:08,678 --> 01:11:09,877
Hello.

1786
01:11:09,878 --> 01:11:11,677
- Hello. - You're the first one here.

1787
01:11:11,678 --> 01:11:15,078
Right. I should practice more to catch up with you, Yeon Ok.

1788
01:11:16,948 --> 01:11:18,347
Let's begin by warming up...

1789
01:11:18,348 --> 01:11:19,908
- when everyone gets here. - All right.

1790
01:11:19,988 --> 01:11:21,058
I'm all warmed up.

1791
01:11:21,418 --> 01:11:22,788
The machine was so fast.

1792
01:11:23,088 --> 01:11:24,228
I had to run around a lot.

1793
01:11:24,458 --> 01:11:27,458
That's trouble. It'll be bad if she improves too fast.

1794
01:11:27,798 --> 01:11:28,904
I won't be able to play with her.

1795
01:11:28,928 --> 01:11:30,328
(Exemplary member, Ok Table Tennis)

1796
01:11:30,898 --> 01:11:33,068
- Hello. - Welcome.

1797
01:11:33,338 --> 01:11:34,467
- Welcome. - Hello.

1798
01:11:34,468 --> 01:11:36,168
- Hello. - Hey.

1799
01:11:36,368 --> 01:11:37,537
Hello.

1800
01:11:37,538 --> 01:11:39,978
- There are so many members. - Hello.

1801
01:11:40,538 --> 01:11:42,638
In total, there are about 20 members.

1802
01:11:42,838 --> 01:11:44,778
- It's a pretty big club. - Yes.

1803
01:11:45,208 --> 01:11:46,647
